{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad858dc56d1becb9","type":"tool_result","content":"# VoxCPM: Tokenizer-Free TTS for Context-Aware Speech Generation and True-to-Life Voice Cloning\narXiv: 2509.24650\nAuthors: Yixuan Zhou, Guoyang Zeng, Xin Liu, Xiang Li, Renjie Yu, Ziyang Wang, Runchuan Ye, Weiyue Sun, Jiancheng Gui, Kehan Li, Zhiyong Wu, Zhiyuan Liu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose an end-to-end hierarchical architecture that introduces an internal semi-discrete bottleneck to resolve the expressivity-stability trade-off by implicitly separating semantic-prosodic planning from fine-grained acoustic modeling.\n  2. We introduce a residual learning strategy that achieves functional specialization without architectural fragmentation, eliminating dependency on external speech tokenizers and simplifying the training pipeline.\n  3. We demonstrate the efficacy of our approach through large-scale training on 1.8 million hours of bilingual speech, achieving state-of-the-art zero-shot TTS performance among open-source systems with high inference efficiency.\n  4. We provide extensive ablation studies validating the semi-discrete residual representations as crucial for robust and expressive synthesis, and publicly release the code and models to support community development.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ\n===VoxCPM===\n# CosyVoice: A Scalable Multilingual Zero-shot Text-to-speech Synthesizer based on Supervised Semantic Tokens\narXiv: 2407.05407\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Qian Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Kai Hu, Heng Lu, Yexin Yang, Hangrui Hu, Siqi Zheng, Yue Gu, Ziyang Ma, Zhifu Gao, Zhijie Yan\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We are the first to integrate supervised speech tokens into text-to-speech models, enhancing content consistency and speaker similarity in zero-shot voice cloning.\n  2. We propose CosyVoice, a scalable zero-shot TTS synthesis system that combines an LLM for text-to-token generation with a conditional flow matching model for token-to-speech synthesis, forsaking the need for additional phonemizers and forced aligners.\n  3. We refine the quality of generated speech by incorporating the x-vector into the LLM to separate speech modeling into semantic, speaker, and prosody components, and optimize the flow matching process with classifier-free guidance, a cosine scheduler, and masked conditions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-语义\n===CosyVoice1===\n# CosyVoice 3: Towards In-the-wild Speech Generation via Scaling-up and Post-training\narXiv: 2505.17589\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Changfeng Gao, Yuxuan Wang, Fan Yu, Tianyu Zhao, Hao Wang, Xiang Lv, Hui Wang, Chongjia Ni, Xian Shi, Keyu An, Guanrou Yang, Yabin Li, Yanni Chen, Zhifu Gao, Qian Chen, Yue Gu, Mengzhe Chen, Yafeng Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Wen Wang, Jieping Ye\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose a novel speech tokenizer derived from a large audio understanding model via supervised multi-task training to better capture paralinguistic information.\n  2. We introduce a differentiable reward optimization (DiffRO) method for post-training that directly optimizes speech tokens using back-propagation.\n  3. We validate dataset size scaling by expanding training data from ten thousand to one million hours, covering 9 languages and 18 Chinese dialects.\n  4. We demonstrate model size scaling by increasing parameters from 0.5 billion to 1.5 billion, which enhances prosody naturalness and performance on difficult tasks.\n  5. We release the CV3-Eval benchmark for zero-shot speech synthesis in the wild, featuring authentic in-the-wild data across diverse languages, domains, and emotions.\n\nTags: TTS/架构-AR-LLM, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow, TTS/控制-参考语音, TTS/控制-指令合成, TTS/功能-RL优化, TTS/功能-多语言, TTS/功能-方言小语种, TTS/功能-多说话人, 压缩/监督-有监督, 压缩/语义声学-混合\n===CosyVoice3===","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2bac2168-16d3-4b83-9f32-4d7b103b1902","uuid":"515f4b07-e5b7-4d50-9d61-b0e301a4ab2b","timestamp":"2026-08-13T13:36:39.406Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# VoxCPM: Tokenizer-Free TTS for Context-Aware Speech Generation and True-to-Life Voice Cloning\narXiv: 2509.24650\nAuthors: Yixuan Zhou, Guoyang Zeng, Xin Liu, Xiang Li, Renjie Yu, Ziyang Wang, Runchuan Ye, Weiyue Sun, Jiancheng Gui, Kehan Li, Zhiyong Wu, Zhiyuan Liu\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose an end-to-end hierarchical architecture that introduces an internal semi-discrete bottleneck to resolve the expressivity-stability trade-off by implicitly separating semantic-prosodic planning from fine-grained acoustic modeling.\n  2. We introduce a residual learning strategy that achieves functional specialization without architectural fragmentation, eliminating dependency on external speech tokenizers and simplifying the training pipeline.\n  3. We demonstrate the efficacy of our approach through large-scale training on 1.8 million hours of bilingual speech, achieving state-of-the-art zero-shot TTS performance among open-source systems with high inference efficiency.\n  4. We provide extensive ablation studies validating the semi-discrete residual representations as crucial for robust and expressive synthesis, and publicly release the code and models to support community development.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Diffusion, TTS/控制-参考语音, 压缩, 压缩/量化-FSQ\n===VoxCPM===\n# CosyVoice: A Scalable Multilingual Zero-shot Text-to-speech Synthesizer based on Supervised Semantic Tokens\narXiv: 2407.05407\nAuthors: Zhihao Du, Qian Chen, Shiliang Zhang, Kai Hu, Heng Lu, Yexin Yang, Hangrui Hu, Siqi Zheng, Yue Gu, Ziyang Ma, Zhifu Gao, Zhijie Yan\nYear: 2024 | Venue: \nTopic: tts_vc\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We are the first to integrate supervised speech tokens into